{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the bird of prey.</b> A bird [of prey], and likewise \"My heritage has become a hyena's den\" [lit. a bird of prey] (Jeremiah 12:9)." "<b>Upon the carcasses.</b> Upon the bodies." "<b>And he sat.</b> With a dagesh in the shin, in place of the nun that is not pronounced [i.e., וַיֵּשֶׁב from ישב with syameq dissimilation], like יגרש and ישלח [as forms]: he drove the bird of prey away from the carcasses, and likewise ישב רוחו (Psalms 147:18). Or: he caused the carcasses to turn back, to chase away the bird of prey."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {2 "The syntax of the second interpretation is compressed and ambiguous: the infinitive להבריח (\"to chase away\") could modify either the subject's action on the carcasses or the purpose of the turning back; translated hyper-literally to preserve the compression."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:42.639329196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}